  <info>
    <link type="guide" xref="index#settings"/>
    <title type="link" role="trail">Babble Help</title>
    <title type="text">Settings</title>
    <title type="link">Settings</title>
    <desc>Interface text size, refresh, notifications, and the defaults a
    new post starts from.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Settings</title>

  <section id="opening">
    <title>Opening Preferences</title>
    <p>
      <link xref="keys">Ctrl+,</link> opens Preferences and it can be
      searched by typing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="interface">
    <title>Interface</title>
    <p>
      It covers the interface text size and line height, how posts refresh,
      desktop and server notifications, and the defaults a new post
      starts from.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="server">
    <title>Server settings</title>
    <p>
      A few settings only reach as far as your server: default visibility,
      language and content warnings are stored in your server preferences,
      so they follow you to any other Mastodon client.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="remote-media">
    <title>Media from other servers</title>
    <p>
      Your server keeps a copy of the media in the posts it shows you.
      When it has none, the original lives on the author's server, and
      loading it lets that server see your IP address and that you viewed
      it. <gui>Media From
      Other Servers</gui> in the <gui>Media</gui> group of the <gui>Reading</gui>
      page of Preferences
      decides what Babble does: <gui>Ask Each Time</gui> asks each time, with a
      choice to remember the answer, <gui>Always Load</gui> loads the original,
      and <gui>Never Load</gui> does not. Media your server holds is
      never asked about. When the original is not loaded, the viewer
      offers to open it in your browser instead.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="autoplay">
    <title>Autoplay and loading media</title>
    <p>
      Two settings in the <gui>Media</gui> group of the <gui>Reading</gui>
      page of Preferences decide when animated media and video start.
    </p>
    <p>
      <gui>Autoplay Animated Media</gui> is on by default. Animated GIFs
      are muted loops, and when it is off they wait for a click instead of
      playing by themselves. Reduced motion, turned-off animations and
      power saving in your system settings always stop them from playing
      by themselves, even when this setting is on. It does not affect videos
      with sound.
    </p>
    <p>
      <gui>Load Media Automatically</gui> covers video, audio and animated
      GIFs, which are streamed. <gui>Always</gui> loads them at once,
      <gui>Not on Metered Connections</gui> (the default) loads them unless
      your system marks the connection as metered, and <gui>Never</gui>
      waits for you to press <gui>Load Video</gui> or <gui>Load Audio</gui>.
      Images and preview thumbnails always load.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="language">
    <title>Language</title>
    <p>
      Changing the interface language takes effect the next time Babble
      starts.
    </p>
  </section>

</page>